mod:store_rootless_destination_faces;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b8, row 2: the rootless destination's other roads, S1bA). EACH TARGET'S OWN ROAD. A store whose destination has no root
// name under its dereferences and casts (177d2b7 row 2, store_rootless_destination.npk) lands its refs on its targets' own roads too, as a named
// root's store reads its root's: a store a hop or more below the value's own walks each target's chain for the destination's hops below it
// (`rrti_path`: `(<-(<-(is c : @la : @lb))).lp = v` over `HPO->:la = a`); a target with no chain to read, a pointer or slice parameter's pointee
// reached by address (`@p.s`), takes the refs itself; and a one-hop store with no pointer parameter among its targets lands them on each target of
// the indirection's own type (`rrti_is_target`), as `PW->:hp = @h; (<-hp).p = v` lands them on `h`, unless the target is a consuming `pick` binding
// whose store is refused already (`pick_store_refused`, DEF-633). Main recorded nothing on those roads, so a view held across the store, or a free by
// the target's other name, read freed heap or freed it twice. One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main
// (3159ab8) and faults there: 28 read freed heap (236 at -O0 and -O2 on roads 0-2, 97 under the detector) and 17 free it twice (74 on every road and
// under the detector). Each is refused here. The right controls are in tests/backend/programs/store_rootless_destination_faces_ok.npk; the prices in
// store_rootless_destination_prices.npk.
// THE FACES: from 177d2b7's review, the family's forms (`c1ll`, `c1lm`, `c1lp`, `c1ls`, `c1la`, `dw_rl`, `dw_rl1`, `c1l3`, `c1lc`, `c1lf`, `c1lk`,
// `c1lo`, `c1lw`) and DEF-660's `rw_*` family (`rw_cl_c`, `rw_cp_c`, `rw_fr_c`, `rw_ls_c`, `rw_tl_c`); seat S's (`rw_pk_c`, `rw_pp_cb`, `rw_ql_cb`,
// `pk2_c`, `pk2_c_dd`); the attack on S1 (`Ailp-team_156`: `a1_pa1`, `a1_pa2`, `a2_sp`, `a3_hqd`, `f_3hop`, `f_3hop_c2`, `f_arr2`, `f_at1`,
// `f_call2`, `f_dfr`, `f_mix2`, `f_mixp`, `f_sp2`, `gen_c`, `r_pa1`, `rw_bv`, `rw_cast`, `rw_for`, `rx_any`, `rx_for`, `rx_lp`); and the attack on
// S1bA's new line (`j2_fsp2`). Left out as duplicates by text: a144/cells2's `c1la`, `dw_rl` and `dw_rl1` (w6's and w7's are here).
error:E5;
struct:K_c1ll = { int64:k; };
